Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2025 11:54:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 904/954] feat(stm32mp2): use SCMI power state protocol for
 CM33 boot

Use the SCMI power state protocol to advertise TF-M of
shutdown reset and system suspend request.

The SCMI driver is initialized with PSCI service.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git aea85369d5d268cc724d85914aea68ec7489a940 feat(stm32mp2): use SCMI power state protocol for CM33 boot]
Change-Id: Ia8d0e1b830eaa3b262f92f3a2def032c29fce044
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/475540
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
